// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a nested un-annotated map whose ONLY nominal claim sits at the `??`
// DEFAULT of a READ, three statements and one function away from the binding it decides.
// Thirteen lines, no import, no generic, no lambda, one layout twin.
//
// `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics at all and is the ONLY command that misses it;
// `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate` exits 0, `vl build` writes
// the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The two `$type`s are the arm's
//  variant-table heap and the twin's struct-table heap, which `DECISIONS.md` keeps in two
//  namespaces on purpose: "the variant/struct-TABLE seam stays nominal".)
//
// WHY THIS ONE AND NOT ANOTHER. Every carrier in the `synthRetPinAnn` / `synthEmptyListAnn` /
// `synthDstPinAnn` family reads a DELIVERY — a destination binding's annotation, a call
// parameter's, a declared result's, a map value cell's. This program has no delivery at all:
// `l1` goes to an un-annotated `c`, `c` is returned from an un-annotated function, and `d1`'s
// annotation is at a CONSUMPTION. The pin family cannot see it by construction, which is what
// makes it a stable specimen rather than one more shape a rung closes by accident.
//
// MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED: eighteen candidate compilers have now been graded against this exact
// program — the fourteen recorded under silent-class-inventory D158, plus the four this file
// ships beside (the committed-rep element row, the pin's two conduit halves, and the
// argument→parameter hop). **NONE of them moves it.** The two that DO move it are the un-gated
// D156 peel, which is refused because it flips D172's refutation pin from `runs` to invalid
// wasm, and a read-site pin leg (D158's own `dstPinMapRead`), which needs that peel to
// complete the chain and therefore inherits the refusal.
//
// PRE-EXISTING on `54780e0b`, on `1559d80c`, on `ff04d74b` and on `a19a3db7` — not a
// regression from the change this file ships with. Filed as `silent-class-inventory.md` D158.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty. One more live member
// is filed with a runnable witness as D156 (its contested half, D171).
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }
function mk(n: i32) {
  const l1 = Map()
  l1["k1"] = { r: n }
  const c = Map()
  c["k2"] = l1
  return c
}
const d1: {[string]: Circle} = Map()
print(((((mk(7))["k2"] ?? d1))["k1"] ?? { r: 0 }).r)
